---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="alert-notify Documentation: React"
  description="Use alert-notify in React: optional Toaster for config props, React-aware toast with JSX icons, and custom() for React nodes."
  pageTitle="React"
>
  <p>
    <span class="tier helper">Helper</span>
    Optional <code>&lt;Toaster /&gt;</code> near the root syncs config as props.
    Import <code>toast</code> from <code>alert-notify/react</code> when passing JSX icons.
    The React entry is a Client Component (<code>"use client"</code>).
    For a live demo and install snippet, see the <a href="/react">React landing</a>.
  </p>

  <pre class="api"><code>{`import { toast, Toaster, custom } from "alert-notify/react";

export function App() {
  return (
    <>
      <Toaster position="top-right" richColors />
      <button onClick={() => toast.success("Saved")}>Save</button>
      <button
        onClick={() =>
          toast.info("Pay with card", {
            icon: <img src="/card.png" alt="" />,
          })
        }
      >
        With icon
      </button>
      <button
        onClick={() =>
          custom(<div>Custom React content</div>, { autoClose: false })
        }
      >
        Custom
      </button>
    </>
  );
}`}</code></pre>

  <ul class="notes">
    <li>Peer dependencies: react and react-dom &gt;= 17.</li>
    <li>Toaster is optional. The portal still auto-mounts without it.</li>
    <li>Core <code>alert-notify</code> toast accepts <code>string | HTMLElement</code> icons only. Use the React entry for JSX.</li>
    <li>Landing page: <a href="/react">/react</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
